# Design: Tailcat address transport adapter (T121)

## Problem
ADR 0011 replaces the tsnet+Headscale stack with the real
github.com/tailscale/tailcat (v0.7.0). T121 adds only the adapter
behind the existing transport.Hub/transport.Device interfaces; T122
switches the callers and T123 deletes the old stack, so both adapters
must coexist without name clashes.

## Approach
- New package internal/transport/address. The tsnet adapter keeps
  internal/transport/tailcat untouched.
- tailcat.Server.Start picks generated keys and the selected DERP
  region into locals and never writes them back, so NewHub generates
  the node key and pre-shared key itself and persists version, keys,
  and region as JSON (owner-only, 0700 dir/0600 file) through
  durablefile under <state>/tailcat-hub/identity.json. Listen starts
  the server (ctx bounds startup), then saves once; a load failure is
  terminal and never overwritten.
- Region handling: ConnInfo.Addr() strips RegionID/code/name and node
  names, and ParseAddr restores RegionID as index+1, so a parsed
  region is not byte-identical to a configured one. A caller-provided
  Region is saved verbatim; only a region Tailcat picked from the
  default map is taken from ParseAddr of the started address. A
  different configured RegionID on restart is refused because the
  identity pins it.
- The address is a secret (it embeds the pre-shared key): the adapter
  never logs it, errors never echo address or key bytes
  (PresharedKey.UnmarshalText echoes its input, so the identity
  loader decodes through string fields and drops that detail), and
  PublicKey() exposes the nodekey:... diagnostic form. Listen binds
  only inside the tailcat stack on 9027; a regression asserts host
  port 9027 stays free.
- Device wraps tailcat.Client with key.NewNode() per process, binds to
  one hub address for its lifetime, and dials port 9027 with a 20 s
  cap when the caller deadline is later (uploader budget is 60 s).
  Drain passthroughs expose the library's FIN-drain hygiene.

## Key Trade-offs
- Default Logf is discard: library diagnostics stay opt-in so no
  uncontrolled sink can receive secret-bearing lines (TS_DEBUG_ADDR
  would print the address).
- Identity is saved after a successful start, not at construction: a
  first start that never listens persists nothing; a failed save fails
  Listen loudly rather than continue with an unpersisted identity.

